IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa4-removal.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 10, Chapter 1: "Removal" (ss 168 to 169A),
-- lines 2282-2305 of ukpga-2006-46.txt. Layer 1 (the law, objectively).
--
-- SOURCE and HOW TO READ AN ANSWER: as in coa4-requirements.l4. Every branch carries its FALSE-kind or NOTHING-kind comment.
-- "forthwith" (s 169(1)) and "(not exceeding a reasonable length)" (s 169(3)) are open-textured: plain inputs, no number
-- is invented; the court's satisfaction (s 169(5)) is an input the text hands to the court.
-- Naming: every top-level name begins with the label of the provision it implements.

-- ---- s 168: resolution to remove director ---------------------------------------------------------------------

-- (1): "A company may by ordinary resolution at a meeting remove a director before the expiration of his period of office,
-- notwithstanding anything in any agreement between it and him." The ordinary resolution is s 282 (coa7): MAYBE BOOLEAN input.
-- src:2283 | 168 Resolution to remove director
-- src:2284 | (1) A company may by ordinary resolution at a meeting remove a director before the expiration of his period of office, notwithstanding anything in any agreement between it and him.
@ref s 168(1) Resolution to remove director (src:2283-2284)
GIVEN `s 282 the resolution is an ordinary resolution` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      way IS A `Way a resolution is passed`
      `an agreement between the company and the director provides that the director may not be removed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 168(1) the company may by that resolution remove the director before the expiration of the director's period of office` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 282 the resolution is an ordinary resolution`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the resolution is an ordinary resolution is s 282 (coa7)
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A company may by ordinary resolution at a meeting remove a director"; another resolution is outside the grant
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
         CONSIDER way
         WHEN `as a written resolution` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by ordinary resolution at a meeting"; a written resolution is outside the grant
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE -- "notwithstanding anything in any agreement between it and him": the agreement input does not change the answer

-- (2): special notice is required of a resolution to remove a director, or to appoint somebody instead of the director so
-- removed at the meeting at which he is removed.
-- src:2285 | (2) Special notice is required of a resolution to remove a director under this section or to appoint somebody instead of a director so removed at the meeting at which he is removed.
@ref s 168(2) Special notice (src:2285)
GIVEN `the resolution is a resolution to remove a director under section 168` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution is a resolution to appoint somebody instead of a director so removed at the meeting at which he is removed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 168(2) special notice is required of the resolution` MEANS
    IF `the resolution is a resolution to remove a director under section 168` OR `the resolution is a resolution to appoint somebody instead of a director so removed at the meeting at which he is removed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Special notice is required of a resolution to remove a director under this section or to appoint somebody instead of a director so removed at the meeting at which he is removed."

-- (3): "A vacancy created by the removal of a director under this section, if not filled at the meeting at which he is
-- removed, may be filled as a casual vacancy."
-- src:2286 | (3) A vacancy created by the removal of a director under this section, if not filled at the meeting at which he is removed, may be filled as a casual vacancy.
@ref s 168(3) A vacancy created by removal (src:2286)
GIVEN `a vacancy is created by the removal of a director under section 168` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the vacancy is filled at the meeting at which the director is removed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 168(3) the vacancy may be filled as a casual vacancy` MEANS
    IF NOT (`a vacancy is created by the removal of a director under section 168`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A vacancy created by the removal of a director under this section"
    ELSE IF `the vacancy is filled at the meeting at which the director is removed`
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if not filled at the meeting at which he is removed"; a vacancy that was filled is outside the grant, and the text does not say it may not be filled as a casual vacancy (fork F70)
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- (4): the person appointed in place is treated, for determining the time at which he or any other director is to retire,
-- as if he had become director on the day on which the person in whose place he is appointed was last appointed.
-- src:2287 | (4) A person appointed director in place of a person removed under this section is treated, for the purpose of determining the time at which he or any other director is to retire, as if he had become director on the day on which the person in whose place he is appointed was last appointed a director.
@ref s 168(4) The retirement of the person appointed in place of a person removed (src:2287)
GIVEN `the person is appointed director in place of a person removed under section 168` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the person in whose place he is appointed was last appointed a director` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 168(4) the day on which the person appointed in place is treated as having become director, for the time at which a director is to retire` MEANS
    IF `the person is appointed director in place of a person removed under section 168`
    THEN JUST `the day on which the person in whose place he is appointed was last appointed a director`
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person appointed director in place of a person removed under this section"

-- (5)(a): the section does not deprive the person removed of compensation or damages payable in respect of the termination.
-- src:2288 | (5) This section is not to be taken—
-- src:2289 | (a) as depriving a person removed under it of compensation or damages payable to him in respect of the termination of his appointment as director or of any appointment terminating with that as director, or
@ref s 168(5)(a) Compensation or damages (src:2288-2289)
GIVEN `compensation or damages are payable to the person removed in respect of the termination of his appointment as director or of any appointment terminating with that` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 168(5)(a) section 168 deprives the person removed of the compensation or damages` MEANS
    IF `compensation or damages are payable to the person removed in respect of the termination of his appointment as director or of any appointment terminating with that`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section is not to be taken— (a) as depriving a person removed under it of compensation or damages payable to him in respect of the termination of his appointment as director or of any appointment terminating with that as director"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks only of compensation or damages that are payable

-- (5)(b): the section does not derogate from any power to remove a director that exists apart from it.
-- src:2288 | (5) This section is not to be taken—
-- src:2290 | (b) as derogating from any power to remove a director that may exist apart from this section.
@ref s 168(5)(b) Powers to remove a director apart from the section (src:2288 and src:2290)
GIVEN `a power to remove the director exists apart from section 168` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 168(5)(b) section 168 derogates from the power to remove the director that exists apart from the section` MEANS
    IF `a power to remove the director exists apart from section 168`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) as derogating from any power to remove a director that may exist apart from this section"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks only of a power that may exist apart from the section

-- ---- s 169: director's right to protest against removal ---------------------------------------------------------

-- (1): "the company must forthwith send a copy of the notice to the director concerned". "forthwith" gives no number of
-- days: a plain fact. The regulative rule has a MUST and no WITHIN (nothing is invented); see NOTES.md.
-- src:2292 | (1) On receipt of notice of an intended resolution to remove a director under section 168, the company must forthwith send a copy of the notice to the director concerned.
@ref s 169(1) The company must send a copy of the notice to the director (src:2292)
GIVEN `the company has received notice of an intended resolution to remove a director under section 168` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has forthwith sent a copy of the notice to the director concerned` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 169(1) the company has complied with the duty to send a copy of the notice to the director concerned` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the company has received notice of an intended resolution to remove a director under section 168`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "On receipt of notice of an intended resolution to remove a director under section 168"; the subsection says nothing of a company that has not received notice (fork F5)
    ELSE IF `the company has forthwith sent a copy of the notice to the director concerned`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company must forthwith send a copy of the notice to the director concerned"

-- src:2292 | (1) On receipt of notice of an intended resolution to remove a director under section 168, the company must forthwith send a copy of the notice to the director concerned.
@ref s 169(1) The company's duty to send a copy of the notice (regulative rule) (src:2292)
`s 169(1) the company's duty to send a copy of the notice to the director concerned` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `Action of a party` OF Company, Director, "send a copy of the notice to the director concerned"
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- (2): the director is entitled to be heard on the resolution at the meeting, whether or not a member.
-- src:2293 | (2) The director (whether or not a member of the company) is entitled to be heard on the resolution at the meeting.
@ref s 169(2) The director's right to be heard (src:2293)
GIVEN `the resolution is a resolution to remove the director under section 168` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director is a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 169(2) the director is entitled to be heard on the resolution at the meeting` MEANS
    IF `the resolution is a resolution to remove the director under section 168`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- "(whether or not a member of the company)": membership does not change the answer
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The director (whether or not a member of the company) is entitled to be heard on the resolution at the meeting"; the subsection concerns the resolution to remove the director

-- (3): the company shall, unless the representations are received too late, (a) state in any notice of the resolution that
-- representations were made and (b) send a copy to every member to whom notice of the meeting is sent.
-- src:2294 | (3) Where notice is given of an intended resolution to remove a director under that section, and the director concerned makes with respect to it representations in writing to the company (not exceeding a reasonable length) and requests their notification to members of the company, the company shall, unless the representations are received by it too late for it to do so—
-- src:2295 | (a) in any notice of the resolution given to members of the company state the fact of the representations having been made; and
-- src:2296 | (b) send a copy of the representations to every member of the company to whom notice of the meeting is sent (whether before or after receipt of the representations by the company).
@ref s 169(3) Representations in writing (src:2294-2296)
GIVEN `notice is given of an intended resolution to remove a director under section 168` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director concerned makes representations in writing to the company with respect to it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the representations do not exceed a reasonable length` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director requests their notification to members of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the representations are received too late for the company to notify them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 169(3) the company is obliged to state the fact of the representations and send a copy of them to the members` MEANS
    IF       `notice is given of an intended resolution to remove a director under section 168`
         AND `the director concerned makes representations in writing to the company with respect to it`
         AND `the representations do not exceed a reasonable length`
         AND `the director requests their notification to members of the company`
         AND NOT (`the representations are received too late for the company to notify them`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company shall, unless the representations are received by it too late for it to do so"

-- src:2294 | (3) Where notice is given of an intended resolution to remove a director under that section, and the director concerned makes with respect to it representations in writing to the company (not exceeding a reasonable length) and requests their notification to members of the company, the company shall, unless the representations are received by it too late for it to do so—
-- src:2295 | (a) in any notice of the resolution given to members of the company state the fact of the representations having been made; and
@ref s 169(3)(a) State the fact of the representations in the notice (src:2294-2295)
GIVEN `the answer under section 169(3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company states in a notice of the resolution given to members the fact of the representations having been made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 169(3)(a) the company has stated the fact of the representations in the notice of the resolution` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer under section 169(3)`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN IF `the company states in a notice of the resolution given to members the fact of the representations having been made`
                        THEN JUST TRUE
                        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company shall, unless the representations are received by it too late for it to do so— (a) in any notice of the resolution given to members of the company state the fact of the representations having been made"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph says nothing of a case in which the company is not obliged
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the obligation arises is not known

-- src:2294 | (3) Where notice is given of an intended resolution to remove a director under that section, and the director concerned makes with respect to it representations in writing to the company (not exceeding a reasonable length) and requests their notification to members of the company, the company shall, unless the representations are received by it too late for it to do so—
-- src:2296 | (b) send a copy of the representations to every member of the company to whom notice of the meeting is sent (whether before or after receipt of the representations by the company).
@ref s 169(3)(b) Send a copy of the representations to every member (src:2294 and src:2296)
GIVEN `the answer under section 169(3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company sends a copy of the representations to every member of the company to whom notice of the meeting is sent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 169(3)(b) the company has sent a copy of the representations to every member to whom notice of the meeting is sent` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer under section 169(3)`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN IF `the company sends a copy of the representations to every member of the company to whom notice of the meeting is sent`
                        THEN JUST TRUE
                        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "send a copy of the representations to every member of the company to whom notice of the meeting is sent (whether before or after receipt of the representations by the company)"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph says nothing of a case in which the company is not obliged
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the obligation arises is not known

-- src:2294 | (3) Where notice is given of an intended resolution to remove a director under that section, and the director concerned makes with respect to it representations in writing to the company (not exceeding a reasonable length) and requests their notification to members of the company, the company shall, unless the representations are received by it too late for it to do so—
-- src:2295 | (a) in any notice of the resolution given to members of the company state the fact of the representations having been made; and
-- src:2296 | (b) send a copy of the representations to every member of the company to whom notice of the meeting is sent (whether before or after receipt of the representations by the company).
@ref s 169(3) The company's duty to notify the members of the representations (regulative rule) (src:2294-2296)
`s 169(3) the company's duty to state the representations and send a copy of them` MEANS
    (PARTY Company
     MUST `Action of a party` OF Company, Member, "state the fact of the representations in the notice of the resolution"
     HENCE FULFILLED)
    RAND
    (PARTY Company
     MUST `Action of a party` OF Company, Member, "send a copy of the representations to every member to whom notice of the meeting is sent"
     HENCE FULFILLED)

-- (4): if a copy is not sent as required by (3) because received too late or because of the company's default, the director
-- may (without prejudice to the right to be heard orally) require that the representations be read out at the meeting.
-- src:2297 | (4) If a copy of the representations is not sent as required by subsection (3) because received too late or because of the company's default, the director may (without prejudice to his right to be heard orally) require that the representations shall be read out at the meeting.
@ref s 169(4) The director may require the representations to be read out (src:2297)
GIVEN `a copy of the representations is not sent as required by subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is not sent because received too late or because of the company's default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 169(4) the director may require that the representations be read out at the meeting` MEANS
    IF `a copy of the representations is not sent as required by subsection (3)` AND `it is not sent because received too late or because of the company's default`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a copy of the representations is not sent as required by subsection (3) because received too late or because of the company's default, the director may"; the right is given on that event and the text does not say the director may not otherwise require it (fork F71)

-- (5): copies need not be sent, and the representations need not be read out, if the court is satisfied that the rights
-- conferred by the section are being abused. The court's satisfaction is the court's judgment: an input.
-- src:2298 | (5) Copies of the representations need not be sent out and the representations need not be read out at the meeting if, on the application either of the company or of any other person who claims to be aggrieved, the court is satisfied that the rights conferred by this section are being abused.
@ref s 169(5) Abuse of the rights (src:2298)
GIVEN `on the application either of the company or of any other person who claims to be aggrieved, the court is satisfied that the rights conferred by section 169 are being abused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 169(5) copies need not be sent out and the representations need not be read out` MEANS
    IF `on the application either of the company or of any other person who claims to be aggrieved, the court is satisfied that the rights conferred by section 169 are being abused`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "need not be sent out and the representations need not be read out at the meeting if, on the application either of the company or of any other person who claims to be aggrieved, the court is satisfied that the rights conferred by this section are being abused"

-- (6): the court may order the company's costs on an application under (5) to be paid by the director, though not a party.
-- src:2299 | (6) The court may order the company's costs (in Scotland, expenses) on an application under subsection (5) to be paid in whole or in part by the director, notwithstanding that he is not a party to the application.
@ref s 169(6) Costs (src:2299)
GIVEN `the application is an application under subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director is a party to the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 169(6) the court may order the company's costs to be paid in whole or in part by the director` MEANS
    IF `the application is an application under subsection (5)`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- "notwithstanding that he is not a party to the application": being a party does not change the answer
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on an application under subsection (5)"

-- ---- s 169A: removal from office of disqualified directors ---------------------------------------------------

-- src:2300 | 169A Removal from office of disqualified directors
-- src:2301 | (1) A person who has been appointed as a director of a company ceases to hold office by virtue of that appointment if the person becomes disqualified under the directors disqualification legislation (see section 159A(2)).
@ref s 169A(1) Removal from office of disqualified directors (src:2300-2301)
GIVEN `the person has been appointed as a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 159A(2) the person becomes disqualified under the directors disqualification legislation` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 169A(1) the person has ceased to hold office by virtue of the appointment` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the person has been appointed as a director of the company`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person who has been appointed as a director of a company ceases to hold office by virtue of that appointment"
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 159A(2) the person becomes disqualified under the directors disqualification legislation`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the person becomes disqualified under the directors disqualification legislation"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is disqualified is s 159A(2), which the caller has not answered

-- src:2302 | (2) Nothing in this section affects any liability of a person under any provision of the Companies Acts or any other enactment, if, having ceased to hold office by virtue of subsection (1), the person—
-- src:2303 | (a) purports to act as director, or
-- src:2304 | (b) acts as shadow director.
@ref s 169A(2) Liability of a person who has ceased to hold office (src:2302-2304)
GIVEN `the person has ceased to hold office by virtue of subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person purports to act as director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts as shadow director` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 169A(2) section 169A leaves the person's liability unaffected` MEANS
    IF `the person has ceased to hold office by virtue of subsection (1)` AND (`the person purports to act as director` OR `the person acts as shadow director`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if, having ceased to hold office by virtue of subsection (1), the person— (a) purports to act as director, or (b) acts as shadow director"

-- (3): for a person appointed before the section came into force, a person "who becomes disqualified" includes one who, at that
-- time, is already disqualified: "includes", so the case it names is JUST TRUE and any other is NOTHING.
-- src:2305 | (3) In relation to a person appointed as a director of a company before the time when this section comes into force, the reference in subsection (1) to a person who becomes disqualified includes a reference to a person who, at that time, is already disqualified.
@ref s 169A(3) Persons appointed before the section comes into force (src:2305)
GIVEN `the person was appointed as a director before the time when section 169A comes into force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person at that time is already disqualified under the directors disqualification legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 169A(3) the person is treated as a person who becomes disqualified` MEANS
    IF `the person was appointed as a director before the time when section 169A comes into force` AND `the person at that time is already disqualified under the directors disqualification legislation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "the reference in subsection (1) to a person who becomes disqualified includes a reference to a person who, at that time, is already disqualified"
